 * `[TYP-15]` *(changed in 0.9.9)* **Where views may be stored.** A view value may be stored only in a
   place whose lifetime is bounded by every region the view carries. Locals, parameters, return values,
   and fields of other view types are bounded. Class fields, statics, `Box` and `Shared` contents,
-  heap-collection elements and `owned fn` captures are not bounded, so they may hold only views whose
-  every region is `static` — which admits string literals, `bytes` literals and views of `static`
-  items: `names = ["ann", "bob"]` is an `Array[str]` of static strings. Any other stored view is
-  `E3063 stored view may not outlive its source`, shape B12.
+  heap-collection elements (an `Array`'s, a `Map`'s keys and values, a `Set`'s elements), a span's
+  elements and `owned fn` captures are not bounded, so they may hold only views whose every region is
+  `static` — which admits string literals, `bytes` literals and views of `static` items: `names =
+  ["ann", "bob"]` is an `Array[str]` of static strings, and a view copied out of such storage is
+  `static` too. Any other stored view is `E3063 stored view may not outlive its source`, shape B12.
+  The rule is about the stored value, wherever the store happens (ODR-069):
+  * a view stored through a `mut` parameter or a reference is stored in the place it points to, which
+    carries the view's regions afterwards (`[LT-21]`): `mem.replace(name, v)` and `put(name, v)` for
+    `fn put(mut x: str, v: str): x = v` leave `name` borrowing what `v` borrows;
+  * a function that stores a view it was given where only a `static` view may go, or into the place a
+    `mut` parameter points to, passes that to its callers: a call must give it a `static` view there
+    (`E3063` at the call otherwise), or is taken to store the view in the argument's place. So a
+    generic `Map[str, V].insert(k, v)` takes a literal key and refuses one borrowed from a local;
+  * a function called where its callers are not checked — a virtual method, a closure, a function
+    value, a `dyn` interface's method — must store only `static` views there, or views already in
+    that place.
 * `[TYP-15a]` The arena-backed containers (`ArenaArray`, `ArenaMap`, §IX.2) and the view containers
   `BorrowList[T]` may hold views bounded by the container's own region.
 
